But they don't just plant trees.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.270
One of the projects
they're currently backing

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:35.370
is a pilot study in Scotland

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:37.800
called enhanced mineral weathering.

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:40.980
So the way it works is they
spread small basalt rocks

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:43.980
throughout forested areas,
and then when it rains

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:46.680
those raindrops contain dissolved CO2

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:48.450
in the form of carbonic acid,

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.280
and when the rain hits the basalt

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:53.310
it reacts and the pH increases.

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:56.130
Now that turns carbonic
acid into carbonates,

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:59.580
like calcium carbonate,
and that precipitates out.

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:01.290
So in this solid mineral form,

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:04.500
the carbon is trapped, potentially
for thousands of years.

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:06.930
And this is the kind
of chemical innovation

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:09.420
we may need to solve the climate crisis.

